.env*.local
# Regenerated by Next on every `dev` and `build`, and dev/build write DIFFERENT
# paths into it (`.next/dev/types/…` vs `.next/types/…`), so a tracked copy is
# dirty after any dev-server start and fails `format:check` on top. Nothing
# needs the committed file: `tsc --noEmit` passes without it, and the Docker
# build runs `next build`, which writes it.
client/web/next-env.d.ts
# Generated at build time by @mantle/app-build's build-runtime (npm: @crossworks/app-build)
client/web/public/app-runtime/
# Written and re-added by `next dev` (node_modules/next/dist/server/lib/
# generate-agent-files.js): AGENTS.md is one delimited block of Next's own
# coding-agent guidance, CLAUDE.md is a single `@AGENTS.md` include. The file's
# own text says committing it keeps the tree clean, and that is true on ONE
# machine — across two it means whichever box last ran `next dev` rewrites the
# block from ITS installed Next, so the pair drifts with the dependency rather
# than with anything anybody wrote. Same reasoning as next-env.d.ts above:
# regenerated on demand, so nothing needs the committed copy.
client/web/AGENTS.md
client/web/CLAUDE.md
# Electron: the staged copy of the built owner UI + packaged artifacts
client/desktop/ui/
client/desktop/release/
# e2e run output: the minted credentials + screenshots, and Playwright's traces
e2e/.artifacts/
e2e/test-results/
